SUMMARY:Quid of Braid Groups and Homological Representations
DESCRIPTION:Given a group G\, it is natural to ask whether or not it is linear\, i.e.\, if G is isomorphic to a subgroup of GL N (R) for some N and some ring R. In this seminar\, we will answer this question for the group G = B n \, the braid group in n strands. Starting from first principles\, we will review the main ideas behind Bigelow's proof of the linearity of B n . Doing so should take us through a pleasant \nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17403/
