SUMMARY:Uniqueness\, symmetry and nodal sets for a Ginzburg–Landau type problem in an infinite strip
DESCRIPTION:The Ginzburg-Landau energy is studied in a specific geometry: an infinite strip with Neumann boundary conditions and under symmetry properties related to very experiments in Bose Einstein condensates. We show that there is a unique minimizer when the width of the strip is below an explicit threshold. This solution is in fact a one dimensional soliton. Above the threshold\, the soliton becomes unsta\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16692/
