SUMMARY:Origami Tori
DESCRIPTION:An origami torus is a piecewise affine isometric embedding of a flat torus into R 3 . It is surprising that these things exist\, but thanks to the work of Burago and Zalgaller in 1960 they do. 30 years later\, B&Z proved that every flat torus is realized as an origami torus. In 2023\, Lazarus and Tallerie proved that you can realize all flat tori using a single underlying triangulation with about 250\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17062/
